  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training in Agroecological Culture for the Rooting of the Indigenous Pa Tavytera of the Amamabay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">APTR will work with approximately 17 indigenous communities in the departments of Amambay, Canindey, and San Pedro to improve agricultural production including cultivation and conservation of traditional seeds for better food security. APTR will also work with communities to protect their local environments, strengthen their cultural identities and enhance the association&apos;s own ability to represent community interests and advocate for rights under Paraguayan law. Approximately 1,600 people will benefit directly.</narrative>
  </description>
